    "result": "`plan_extraction` is implemented in `solution.py`, and the 21 tests in `tests/test_solution.py` pass with `python -m pytest -q tests`.\n\nIt follows every rule in `spec.md`. That covers the checks on the raw member name (NUL, leading separator, drive prefix) and the normalisation of `/` and `\\` separators, `.` segments and `..` segments. Directory entries are checked but left out of the result. Collisions between file members are caught case-insensitively. If any member is unsafe it raises without returning a partial plan.\n\nI made two judgement calls where the spec is silent. Directory entries don't count toward name collisions, since rule 6 says \"file members\". A non-string member raises `UnsafePathError`.",
